  "query_preview": "/Tuesday through Saturday/...\nIssued 353 AM MDT SAT OCT 17 2026\nThrough much of the work week, the upper-level low pressure \nsystem will move from just off the California coast to lingering\nin the Great Basin. Temperatures will cool off Tuesday as\nanother weak front moves into the region along with increasing \ncloud cover during the day. Models are split on fully moving the\nfront through the area or having it stall out in southwest ID. \nRegardless, temperatures will cool down to near- normal in \nsoutheast OR and around 5 degrees above normal in southwest ID. \nFlow aloft through much of the week will be out of the south, \ngradually increasing PWATs through at least Thursday. This, \nalong with favorable topographic effects, will introduce \nwidespread precipitation chances Wednesday afternoon into \nThursday.\n\nEnsemble guidance largely favors another cold front late \nThursday into Friday as another upper-level trough moves into \nthe Pacific NW and BC, Canada. This feature will have the low \nrejoin the broader flow and move east through the day Friday. \nThis will lead to even colder temperatures going into next \nweekend. The synoptic pattern with the next trough is too \nuncertain to discuss Saturday any further at this time.",
